      "writtenOn": "2025-02-19T18:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m picking this CL up as it\u0027s needed to enable trusty FDs to be transferred between a trusty binder rpc session and a trusty binder rpc server.\n\nI can think of a couple of ways forward on this concern. They\u0027re stated here in order of my preference, but please let me know what you think. I don\u0027t have as much insight into the history or planned future for binder to know what\u0027s best.\n\n1. Add a static assert that ARpcServer is an empty struct. This gives some level of confidence that this cast continues to be safe as long as ARpcServer remains empty and if `ArpcServer` ever changes, we\u0027ll know it breaks this function at compile time. Of course, this could kick the can down the road. If `ARpcServer` changes, we\u0027ll need to find a way to do this conversion safely.\n\n2. Have `RpcServer` expose methods to translate from `ARpcServer` and back. Currently these methods are an implementation detail [1] of `ARpcServer`, but exposing them would allow us to avoid assuming how to convert between the two.\n\n3. Don\u0027t take this approach of trying to resolve and delegate to `ARpcServer` from `ARpcServerTrusty`. Instead, implement `ARpcServerTrusty_setSupportedFileDescriptorTransportMode` directly. Note this essentially involves copying `ARpcServer_setSupportedFileDescriptorTransportMode` [2].\n\n[1]https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/libbinder_rpc_unstable.cpp;l\u003d43-61;drc\u003daee4e9d7b750d88b048ae74e371e2859a788fdc6\n\n[2]https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/native/libs/binder/libbinder_rpc_unstable.cpp;l\u003d157;drc\u003daee4e9d7b750d88b048ae74e371e2859a788fdc6",
      "parentUuid": "347cfe7d_e304596d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 76,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 65
