      "writtenOn": "2025-02-20T03:04:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, I see so it should be okay, but could you consider to avoid reinterpret_cast then:\n- `struct ARpcServer {};` -\u003e `struct ARpcServer;` (use declaration)\n- here, you can probably \u0027using ARpcServer \u003d RpcServer*;` or similar to work around it.\n\nGenerally though, the implementation of an API type should be a single concrete implementation, defined once. If it is defined multiple times in different translation units, you get an effective reinterpret_cast between types of the same name and it will violate ODR rule. Though, this is a more fundamental issue, nothing we can do about it.",
